From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel's intern <intern@thingy.jp>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sw-sdl2: don't request an OpenGL window for the software
 renderer

The SDL software renderer only ever uses SDL_Renderer / SDL_Texture; it
never creates a GL context. Requesting SDL_WINDOW_OPENGL is therefore
unnecessary. It is harmless on video drivers that expose OpenGL, but on a
GL-less driver such as DirectFB2 (which dropped the GL module) it makes
SDL_CreateWindow() fail outright - the emulator then keeps running with a
NULL window/renderer and never shows a picture.

Drop the flag so the software frontend gets a normal window and displays
on GL-less targets.

Signed-off-by: Daniel's intern <intern@thingy.jp>
---
--- a/src/platform/sdl/sw-sdl2.c	2026-07-29 09:26:51.713734118 +0000
+++ b/src/platform/sdl/sw-sdl2.c	2026-07-29 09:26:51.712671294 +0000
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@
 bool mSDLSWInit(struct mSDLRenderer* renderer) {
 	unsigned width, height;
 	renderer->core->desiredVideoDimensions(renderer->core, &width, &height);
-	renderer->window = SDL_CreateWindow(projectName, SDL_WINDOWPOS_UNDEFINED, SDL_WINDOWPOS_UNDEFINED, renderer->viewportWidth, renderer->viewportHeight, SDL_WINDOW_OPENGL | (SDL_WINDOW_FULLSCREEN_DESKTOP * renderer->player.fullscreen));
+	renderer->window = SDL_CreateWindow(projectName, SDL_WINDOWPOS_UNDEFINED, SDL_WINDOWPOS_UNDEFINED, renderer->viewportWidth, renderer->viewportHeight, (SDL_WINDOW_FULLSCREEN_DESKTOP * renderer->player.fullscreen));
 	SDL_GetWindowSize(renderer->window, &renderer->viewportWidth, &renderer->viewportHeight);
 	renderer->player.window = renderer->window;
 	renderer->sdlRenderer = SDL_CreateRenderer(renderer->window, -1, SDL_RENDERER_ACCELERATED | SDL_RENDERER_PRESENTVSYNC);
